:: Meal Prototype Test Run Effect [activity meal] {"position":"1475,2225"}
/*
{
        id: "prototype_test_run_effect",
        passage: "Meal Prototype Test Run Effect",
        isActive: false,
        mealType: ["breakfast"],
        isImportant: true,
        dayType: ["weekday", "weekend"],
        cooldown: 0,
        once: true,
        lastSeen: -1,
        present: ["mom", "sister"],
        requirements: [
        ],
        set: [
            () => setup.getMealById("prototype_test_run_effect").isActive = false,
        ]
}
   Activated by: "Prototype Breakthrough" (main_breakthrough), the morning after the first test run
   and after I caught her keeping her promise.
*/
$mom.callName is humming.

That's the first thing I notice when I come down. Not the smell of coffee or the pan of eggs, but the humming, some old song from the radio that she gets half the words wrong to. She's standing at the stove in her robe with her hair still damp, flipping eggs with a little flourish, and she looks like someone who slept nine hours and woke up before the alarm.

/* IMAGE: images/meals/important/prototype_test_run_effect.jpg | Morning kitchen. Mom at the stove in her robe, damp hair, relaxed smile. Sister at the table squinting at her suspiciously over a mug. */

$sister.callName is already at the table, both hands around her mug, watching her like she's a nature documentary.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "Okay, what happened to you?" },
{ who: $mom, text: "What do you mean? Nothing happened. Eggs?" },
{ who: $sister, text: "You're humming. You never hum. You made eggs on a weekday. Your face looks... rested. It's honestly a little scary." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Can't a woman get a good night's sleep without being interrogated in her own kitchen?" },
{ who: $sister, text: "Not when she's been a zombie for three months, no." },
{ text: "$mom.callName slides a plate in front of me. Our eyes meet for exactly one second before she looks at the toaster like it just said something interesting. The color starts at her collarbone and climbs." },
{ who: $mom, text: "I just... took some time for myself last night. That's all. Somebody suggested I should do that more often." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

$sister.callName looks from her to me and back, eyebrows up, then shrugs and goes back to her phone. She's decided it's a boring grown-up thing. She's half right.

I eat my eggs. They're perfect, which they never are, and I can't remember the last time $mom.callName burned nothing at all.

<div id="mtre-choice">
<<link "Ask her if the relaxation helped">><<replace "#mtre-choice">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "So that relaxation thing we talked about. Did it help?" },
{ text: "The spatula stops in mid-air. $sister.callName doesn't look up from her phone, thank god." },
{ who: $mom, text: "It... yes. It did. Eat your breakfast, $player.name." },
{ text: "She turns back to the stove and doesn't hum again until I've left the kitchen. But when I glance back from the doorway, she's smiling at the pan." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>
<<UpdateStat "+" "MomCorruption" 1>>
<<UpdateStat "+" "MomLust" 5>>
<</replace>><</link>>
<<link "Just compliment the eggs">><<replace "#mtre-choice">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "These are really good, $mom.callName. Like, restaurant good." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Oh, stop. They're just eggs." },
{ who: $sister, text: "They're suspiciously good eggs." },
{ text: "$mom.callName flicks a dish towel at her, and the humming starts up again, a little louder than before." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>
<<UpdateStat "+" "MomRelation" 2>>
<</replace>><</link>>
</div>
